s, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{ln}⁡[(0.7)^{x+9}] & \\ge \\operatorname{ln}⁡2 \\\\ (x+9)\\operatorname{ln}⁡0.7 & \\ge \\operatorname{ln}⁡2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLastly, note that $\\operatorname{ln}⁡0.7$ is a negative quantity, so when we divide both sides by it, we need to flip the inequality:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x+9 & \\le \\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡0.7} \\\\ x & \\le \\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡0.7}-9\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534206 true] [17592186282205 1000 #edb/ref 17592186282206 13194139534206 true] [17592186282205 1000 #edb/ref 17592186282207 13194139534206 true] [17592186282205 1000 #edb/ref 17592186282208 13194139534206 true] [17592186282205 1000 #edb/ref 17592186282209 13194139534206 true] [17592186282205 1000 #edb/ref 17592186282210 13194139534206 true] [17592186282205 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534206 true] [17592186282205 1041 "selection" 13194139534206 true] [17592186282205 1104 #edb/ref 17592186282208 13194139534206 true] [17592186282205 1110 #uuid "e11fd5a1-6666-52f1-95ec-ed1f9256af9e" 13194139534206 true] [17592186282206 1034 "x\\le \\frac{9}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡0.7}-2" 13194139534206 true] [17592186282206 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534206 true] [17592186282206 1111 #uuid "31524f6f-9455-5698-839b-7c8011f5f2fa" 13194139534206 true] [17592186282207 1034 "x\\ge \\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡0.7}-3" 13194139534206 true] [17592186282207 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534206 true] [17592186282207 1111 #uuid "3101d6b6-76c6-5bfd-9ca7-5e4ce12c4c33" 13194139534206 true] [17592186282208 1034 "x\\le \\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡0.7}-9" 13194139534206 true] [17592186282208 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534206 true] [17592186282208 1111 #uuid "d46004f7-34ec-5bd0-b351-1705c4d16eac" 13194139534206 true] [17592186282209 1034 "x\\ge \\frac{3}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡0.7}+2" 13194139534206 true] [17592186282209 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 131